{"jobs":[{"job":"filing_a_debit_card_transaction_dispute","into":["filing_a_debit_card_transaction_dispute"],"aliases":["ATM cash discrepancy dispute","Reg E dispute","Rho-Bank ATM cash claim the record does not support","Rho-Bank ATM deposit not fully credited","atm_dispute_special_procedures","customer asks for a human agent before filing debit disputes","debit card dispute","debit disputes on a Premium card (duplicate, overcharge) and an Entry card holding an open dispute (P2P fraud held back, late-reported in-store fraud filed)","debit_card_dispute","dispute an unrecognized charge found during a chip/CVV or fraud-alert transaction review","dispute several fraudulent out-of-state ATM withdrawals found on a PIN-locked card","dispute successful unauthorized transactions found during a PIN lock investigation","disputed amount the customer states differs from the transaction record","duplicate charge with no merchant contact still gets required provisional credit","duplicate debit charge dispute","file_debit_card_transaction_dispute","four debit disputes on two cards: duplicate and overcharge on a Premium account, P2P fraud and late-reported in-store fraud on an Entry account already holding an open dispute","fraudulent EveryonePay / P2P transfer on a debit card","fraudulent in-store charge found during a customer-initiated fraud alert review on a declined card","goods or services not received on a debit card","incorrect amount (overcharge) on a debit card","late-reported debit card fraud","late-reported in-person fraud on a card the customer still holds, with the P2P fraud dispute deferred by the open-dispute limit","multiple debit card disputes","multiple debit disputes across several cards","no dispute when a PIN-locked card shows only declined attempts","online order never delivered on a debit card","open-dispute limit reached on a checking account","recurring_payment_dispute","reg_e_dispute","several debit disputes on two checking accounts handled one at a time","several disputes on two debit cards with a mix of categories","subscription charged after cancellation on a debit card","third-party ATM dispute","unauthorized debit transaction by a family member","unauthorized_debit_transaction_on_a_lost_card","debit_card_action_after_dispute","freeze or close debit card after dispute","ordering_a_replacement_debit_card","reissue debit card after fraud closure"],"when":{"quote":"When a customer needs to file a dispute for a debit card transaction (unauthorized charges, ATM errors, merchant issues, or incorrect amounts), the agent must gather comprehensive information and follow Regulation E requirements.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},"starts":{"by":"customer","note":"customer: start only when the customer asks to dispute one or more debit card transactions. This includes a customer who, during a transaction review in another job, denies a transaction and agrees when the agent advises filing a dispute. Such reviews are a chip/CVV mismatch, a fraud alert, or the PIN lock investigation's check for successful unauthorized transactions on a card that cannot be unlocked.

File one dispute for each transaction the customer names. Card actions (a freeze, or a close and reissue) are not optional offers. They follow from the categories of the disputes actually filed, as the dispute procedure requires. A dispute held back by the open-dispute limit, or dropped by the customer after a record check, sets no card action.

If the customer opens by asking for a human agent, offer to help first, as the policy says. Transfer only on the 4th request.","quote":"When a customer needs to file a dispute for a debit card transaction (unauthorized charges, ATM errors, merchant issues, or incorrect amounts), the agent must gather comprehensive information and follow Regulation E requirements.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},"tools":[{"tool":"get_user_information_by_name","who":"agent","step":"lookup_user","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_user_information_by_email","who":"agent","step":"lookup_user","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_user_information_by_id","who":"agent","step":"lookup_user","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_current_time","who":"agent","step":"get_time","not_used":null},{"tool":"log_verification","who":"agent","step":"log_verification","not_used":null},{"tool":"unlock_discoverable_agent_tool","who":"agent","step":"get_accounts","not_used":null},{"tool":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","who":"agent","step":"get_accounts","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_all_user_accounts_by_user_id_3847","who":"agent","step":"get_accounts","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823","who":"agent","step":"get_cards","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_bank_account_transactions_9173","who":"agent","step":"get_transactions","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_debit_dispute_status_7483","who":"agent","step":"get_dispute_status","not_used":null},{"tool":"get_atm_deposit_images_8473","who":"agent","step":"atm_deposit_images","not_used":null},{"tool":"file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281","who":"agent","step":"file_dispute","not_used":null},{"tool":"freeze_debit_card_3892","who":"agent","step":"freeze_card","not_used":null},{"tool":"unfreeze_debit_card_3893","who":"agent","step":"unfreeze_before_close","not_used":null},{"tool":"close_debit_card_4721","who":"agent","step":"close_card","not_used":null},{"tool":"order_debit_card_5739","who":"agent","step":"order_replacement","not_used":null},{"tool":"transfer_to_human_agents","who":"agent","step":"transfer_if_needed","not_used":null},{"tool":"set_debit_card_recurring_block_7382","who":"agent","step":null,"not_used":"Blocking future recurring charges is a separate job, block_recurring_payments. It runs after the dispute, and only if the customer wants future charges stopped on a card that stays open."},{"tool":"get_credit_card_accounts_by_user","who":"agent","step":null,"not_used":"The credit card check after a lost or stolen debit card belongs to lost_stolen_card_cross_product_security_protocol (see cross_product_handoff)."},{"tool":"close_bank_account_7392","who":"agent","step":null,"not_used":"Doc 005 is cited only for its list of account names by tier. A dispute never closes a checking account."},{"tool":"clear_debit_card_fraud_alert_4892","who":"agent","step":null,"not_used":"A fraud alert on a card with a denied transaction is never cleared. The card is closed through its card action instead (alert_card_no_clear)."},{"tool":"apply_checking_account_credit_5829","who":"agent","step":null,"not_used":"This tool is only for missing rebates and fee mischarges (doc 017). Dispute provisional credit is recorded only through the provisional_credit_eligible argument of file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281, so this tool is never used for a dispute."}],"info":[{"field":"identity_values","about":"Two of: date of birth, email, phone, address. They must match the record found by name, email or user id.","from":"customer","ask":"To verify your identity, could you give me your full name and two of the following: date of birth, email, phone number, or address on file?","may_hold_back":false},{"field":"card_last_4_and_account","about":"Which debit card or checking account each disputed transaction is on","from":"customer","ask":"Which debit card (last 4 digits) or checking account is this transaction on?","may_hold_back":false},{"field":"transaction_details","about":"The merchant or payee (or ATM), date and amount of each disputed transaction, used to find its transaction_id","from":"customer","ask":"What were the merchant, date and amount of the transaction you want to dispute?","may_hold_back":false},{"field":"issue_description","about":"What went wrong: duplicate, wrong amount, not received, recurring after cancellation, ATM cash or deposit, or a transaction they did not make (then ask whether fraud is suspected). This sets dispute_category.","from":"customer","ask":"What is wrong with this transaction? Did you make it, or do you think it is fraud?","may_hold_back":false},{"field":"expected_amount","about":"For incorrect_amount: the amount the customer should have been charged. The disputed amount is the difference from the posted charge.","from":"customer","ask":"What amount should you have been charged for this purchase?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"fraud_suspected","about":"For an unauthorized transaction: whether fraud by an unknown party is suspected, or someone the customer knows (e.g. a family member) used the card without permission","from":"customer","ask":"Do you know who made this transaction, for example a family member, or do you suspect fraud by someone you don't know?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"card_lost_or_stolen","about":"Whether the card was lost or stolen and not yet reported. This decides card_in_possession, the close reason and the cross-product check.","from":"customer","ask":"Do you still have this card, or has it been lost or stolen?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"atm_owner","about":"For an ATM dispute: whether it was a Rho-Bank ATM or a third-party ATM","from":"customer","ask":"Was this a Rho-Bank ATM or a third-party ATM, such as one in a store?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"amount_not_received","about":"For an ATM cash discrepancy: how much cash the machine actually gave out, compared with the amount requested","from":"customer","ask":"How much did you request, and how much cash did the machine actually give you?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"deposit_amount_claimed","about":"For a Rho-Bank ATM deposit dispute: how much the customer says they deposited, compared with what was credited","from":"customer","ask":"How much did you deposit at the ATM, and how much was credited to your account?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"transaction_type","about":"How the transaction was made: PIN purchase, signature purchase, online purchase, ATM withdrawal, ATM deposit, recurring payment, or person-to-person transfer","from":"customer","ask":"Was this an in-store purchase with a PIN or a signature, an online or phone purchase, an ATM transaction, a recurring payment, or a person-to-person transfer?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"discovery_date","about":"The date the customer first noticed the issue (MM/DD/YYYY). If the customer says 'today', use the date from get_current_time.","from":"customer","ask":"On what date did you first notice this issue?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"card_in_possession","about":"Whether the customer still has the physical debit card","from":"customer","ask":"Do you still have your physical debit card in your possession?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"pin_compromised","about":"yes_shared, yes_observed, no or unknown","from":"customer","ask":"Do you believe your PIN may have been compromised?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"contacted_merchant","about":"Whether the customer tried to resolve it with the merchant (required for non-fraud disputes)","from":"customer","ask":"Have you attempted to resolve this directly with the merchant?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"police_report_filed","about":"Whether a police report was filed. Asked for fraud disputes over $500, or answered when the customer raises it.","from":"customer","ask":"Have you filed a police report about this?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"written_statement_agreed","about":"Whether the customer agrees that this conversation serves as their written statement. Asked once per conversation and reused for every dispute.","from":"customer","ask":"Are you willing to provide a written statement describing what happened? We can use this conversation as your written statement if you agree.","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"still_dispute_after_record_check","about":"When the recorded amount differs from what the customer said, or a Rho-Bank ATM record shows the cash was dispensed correctly: whether the customer still wants the dispute filed","from":"customer","ask":"Our records show this transaction for a different amount than you mentioned. Would you still like to dispute it?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"dispute_priority_choice","about":"When the account's open-dispute limit leaves room for fewer disputes than requested: which ones the customer wants filed now","from":"customer","ask":"This account can only take a limited number of open disputes right now. Which transaction would you like to file first?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"replacement_choice","about":"Only when a card is closed (close_and_reissue): whether the customer wants a replacement now, plus the delivery option, card design and mailing address","from":"customer","ask":"Would you like me to order a replacement card now? Which delivery option and card design would you like, and where should we mail it?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"wants_future_recurring_block","about":"For a recurring charge after cancellation: whether the customer also wants all future recurring charges on the card blocked","from":"customer","ask":"Would you also like to stop future recurring charges on this card, or just dispute this charge?","may_hold_back":true},{"field":"accounts_cards_transactions_disputes","about":"From the records:
- checking accounts: account_id, account_class/tier, status, balance, date_opened;
- debit cards: card_id, last 4, status, issue_reason, date_issued;
- transactions: transaction_id, date, amount, type, description, status;
- existing debit disputes: account_id, status.","from":"records","ask":"","may_hold_back":false}],"steps":[{"id":"request_human","by":"model","do":"If the customer asks for a human agent while the request is one you can handle (filing debit disputes and the card actions), say politely that you can help with this yourself, and continue the workflow. Count every request for a human in the conversation.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":[],"after":[],"if":"the customer asks for a human agent","quote":"If an issue falls within your capabilities and the user still wants to be transferred to a human agent, kindly inform the user that you can help them, and try to help them first.","doc":"policy"},{"id":"transfer_on_fourth_request","by":"model","do":"On the customer's 4th request for a human, call transfer_to_human_agents with a summary of the verification and the disputes filed so far. Choose the reason code from the highest tier that applies: fraud_or_security_concern when unauthorized or fraudulent transactions are involved, otherwise the best-matching code.","call":"transfer_to_human_agents","args":{"summary":"model summary of the verification status, the disputes filed and anything still pending","reason":"the highest-tier reason code that applies (doc 042)"},"lookup":["request_human"],"after":["request_human"],"if":"the customer has asked for a human agent 4 times","quote":"If the user asks for a human agent 4 times, then you may invoke the transfer_to_human_agents tool.","doc":"policy"},{"id":"from_review_handoff","by":"model","do":"If this job starts from a transaction review in another job (chip/CVV mismatch, fraud alert, stolen card), reuse the verification and the accounts, cards and transactions already read. Skip greet through log_verification, and re-read a record only if it is missing. Then continue at get_dispute_status.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":[],"after":[],"if":"the customer was already verified in this conversation and denied a transaction during a review in another job","quote":"No need to verify more than once in a single conversation.","doc":"policy"},{"id":"from_pin_lock_handoff","by":"model","do":"This job can start from the PIN lock investigation's cannot-unlock path, where successful transactions in the suspicious period are ones the customer confirms were not theirs. Reuse the verification and the records already read, and continue at get_dispute_status. These are fraud disputes:
- card_present_fraud for an ATM withdrawal or in-store purchase made with the physical card or PIN (transaction_type atm_withdrawal or pin_purchase);
- card_not_present_fraud for an online or phone transaction.
Record card_in_possession from the customer (true if they still hold the card). Record pin_compromised from their answer ('unknown' if unsure). The card action (close_and_reissue) then runs in decide_card_action and close_card.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions","get_cards"],"after":[],"if":"the job starts from the PIN lock investigation's cannot-unlock path and the customer confirms successful transactions in the suspicious period were not theirs","quote":"If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute, close card, order replacement.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"id":"pin_lock_no_unauthorized_no_dispute","by":"model","do":"The PIN lock investigation's check may find only declined attempts on a card that cannot be unlocked, with no successful unauthorized transactions. Declined attempts took no money, so file nothing for that card and do not start this job for it. Tell the customer no money was taken. Then return to the protocol's options: closure and replacement, a security-team transfer, or a PIN reset.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions"],"after":[],"if":"the job would start from the PIN lock investigation but no successful unauthorized transactions were found in the suspicious period","quote":"If no unauthorized transactions: Explain the security concern and offer options:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"id":"pin_lock_each_withdrawal","by":"model","do":"When the PIN lock investigation finds several successful unauthorized transactions in the suspicious period, file one dispute per transaction_id, each with its own amount and date from get_transactions. Do not file one dispute for the total. Before filing, tell the customer the total that was taken.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions"],"after":["from_pin_lock_handoff"],"if":"the PIN lock handoff has more than one successful unauthorized transaction on the card","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"greet","by":"model","do":"Greet the customer and confirm they want to file debit card disputes. Ask for their name (or email) and two of: date of birth, email, phone number, address.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":[],"after":[],"if":null,"quote":"When a customer needs to file a dispute for a debit card transaction (unauthorized charges, ATM errors, merchant issues, or incorrect amounts), the agent must gather comprehensive information and follow Regulation E requirements.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"lookup_user","by":"model","do":"Look up the customer by what they gave: get_user_information_by_name for a name (case sensitive), get_user_information_by_email for an email, get_user_information_by_id for a user id.","call":"get_user_information_by_name","args":{"customer_name":"the name the customer gave"},"lookup":[],"after":["greet"],"if":null,"quote":"Customer must be verified","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"check_identity","by":"model","do":"Confirm that 2 of DOB, email, phone and address match the record. Share no account information before this. If they do not match, ask again. If they still do not match, tell the customer you cannot verify them, and stop.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["lookup_user"],"after":["lookup_user"],"if":null,"quote":"Customer must be verified","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"get_time","by":"harness","do":"Get the current time for the verification log and the date checks.","call":"get_current_time","args":{},"lookup":[],"after":["check_identity"],"if":null,"quote":"Customer must be verified","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"log_verification","by":"harness","do":"Log the verification.","call":"log_verification","args":{"name":"the verified user's name","user_id":"the verified user's id","address":"address from records","email":"email from records","phone_number":"phone from records","date_of_birth":"DOB from records (MM/DD/YYYY)","time_verified":"the time from get_current_time"},"lookup":["check_identity"],"after":["get_time"],"if":"2 or more identity values matched in check_identity","quote":"Customer must be verified","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"one_dispute_at_a_time","by":"model","do":"When the customer wants to go through several disputes one at a time, take the first dispute through the whole path: match it in get_transactions, run the record checks and check_prefiling, gather details, file_dispute and confirm_filed. Then ask for the next dispute. Reuse the verification and the account, card, transaction and dispute-status reads already made, and read another account only when a dispute is on it. Count each dispute filed earlier in this conversation toward its account's open-dispute limit. Ask the written-statement question once (written_statement_reuse). Run decide_card_action only after the customer's last dispute.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_dispute_status","file_dispute"],"after":["log_verification"],"if":"the customer has several disputes and asks to handle them one at a time","quote":"However, when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action across all disputes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"get_accounts","by":"harness","do":"Unlock get_all_user_accounts_by_user_id_3847, then call it to list the checking accounts with their type, class (tier), status, balance and date opened.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"get_all_user_accounts_by_user_id_3847","user_id":"the verified user's id"},"lookup":[],"after":["log_verification"],"if":null,"quote":"Use get_all_user_accounts_by_user_id_3847 to retrieve the bank accounts (checkings, savings) for a customer.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_009"},{"id":"get_cards","by":"harness","do":"Unlock get_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823, then call it for each relevant checking account. Match each card the customer named by its last 4 digits, and note its card_id, account_id and status.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"get_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823","account_id":"each checking account id"},"lookup":[],"after":["get_accounts"],"if":null,"quote":"Use get_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823 to look up all debit cards associated with a specific checking account.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_028"},{"id":"get_transactions","by":"harness","do":"Unlock get_bank_account_transactions_9173, then call it for each relevant account. Find each disputed transaction by description, date and amount. Note its transaction_id, date, amount, type and status.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"get_bank_account_transactions_9173","account_id":"each relevant checking account id"},"lookup":[],"after":["get_accounts"],"if":null,"quote":"Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"find the transaction_id with this tool","quote":"Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"status field shows pending or posted","quote":"Transaction status, either 'posted' or 'pending'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_018"}]},{"id":"match_failed","by":"model","do":"If a card the customer names (by its last 4 digits) is not in get_cards, or a transaction they describe is not in get_transactions, tell them you cannot find it. Ask them to check the card, merchant, date and amount. Never file a dispute for a transaction that is not in the records.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_cards","get_transactions"],"after":["get_cards","get_transactions"],"if":"a named card or a described transaction cannot be matched in the records","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"amount_differs_from_record","by":"model","do":"A transaction may match by merchant (or ATM) and date while its amount in get_transactions differs from the amount the customer said. Tell the customer the recorded amount and ask whether they still want to dispute it.
- If they still want to dispute the whole charge, file it with the recorded amount from get_transactions as disputed_amount.
- For incorrect_amount, the disputed_amount stays the recorded charge minus what the customer says they should have paid (incorrect_amount_branch).
- For an ATM cash discrepancy, the disputed_amount stays the cash not received (decide_parameters).
- If they decide not to dispute it, do not file it. Say it was not filed, and go on to their next dispute. A dispute that was not filed sets no card action.
For a Rho-Bank ATM cash discrepancy, use rho_atm_journal instead.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions"],"after":["get_transactions"],"if":"the charge amount the customer states for a matched transaction differs from the amount in get_transactions, and the dispute is not a Rho-Bank ATM cash discrepancy","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"tell the recorded amount and ask whether they still want to dispute it","source":"none","why":"No passage covers a mismatch between remembered and recorded amounts, so the step asks the customer."},{"clause":"whole-charge dispute uses the recorded amount","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"incorrect_amount disputes the difference","quote":"'incorrect_amount': Charged different amount than expected","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"ATM cash discrepancy disputes the cash not received","quote":"'atm_cash_discrepancy': ATM dispensed wrong amount or no cash","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"not filed sets no card action","quote":"However, when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action across all disputes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]},{"id":"pick_earliest_duplicate","by":"model","do":"For a duplicate charge, dispute the earliest (first) of the matching transactions. The disputed amount is one charge.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_transactions"],"after":["get_transactions"],"if":"the dispute is a duplicate charge","quote":"Dispute the earliest (first) transaction when multiple duplicates exist.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"get_dispute_status","by":"harness","do":"Unlock get_debit_dispute_status_7483, then call it and count the open debit disputes on each account.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"get_debit_dispute_status_7483","user_id":"the verified user's id"},"lookup":[],"after":["log_verification"],"if":null,"quote":"To retrieve a customer's debit card dispute history and check the status of open disputes, use the get_debit_dispute_status_7483 tool.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_035"},{"id":"count_open_disputes","by":"model","do":"From get_dispute_status, group the disputes by account_id.
- Count as still open: OPEN, PENDING_DOCUMENTATION, UNDER_REVIEW and PROVISIONAL_CREDIT_ISSUED.
- Do not count: RESOLVED_CUSTOMER_FAVOR, RESOLVED_BANK_FAVOR, RESOLVED_PARTIAL, PROVISIONAL_REVERSED and CLOSED_NO_RESPONSE.
Use these per-account counts in check_prefiling, even if the customer has not mentioned an earlier dispute.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_dispute_status","get_accounts"],"after":["get_dispute_status"],"if":null,"quote":"OPEN: Dispute filed, investigation in progress","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_035"},{"id":"timeline_escalation","by":"model","do":"An existing dispute in get_dispute_status may have exceeded its regulatory timelines, measured against get_time. That means provisional credit was not issued within 10 business days (20 for new accounts), or the investigation has gone past 45 days (90 for international/POS). If so, tell the customer and offer to escalate it to a supervisor. Call transfer_to_human_agents only if the customer agrees, and only after the new disputes in this conversation are handled.","call":"transfer_to_human_agents","args":{"summary":"the dispute past its timeline and the disputes filed in this conversation","reason":"the highest-tier reason code that applies (doc 042)"},"lookup":["get_dispute_status","get_time"],"after":["count_open_disputes"],"if":"an existing dispute exceeds its regulatory timelines AND the customer agrees to the escalation","quote":"If a dispute appears to be exceeding timelines, escalate to a supervisor.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_035"},{"id":"check_prefiling","by":"model","do":"For each dispute, check the pre-filing rules:
1. The amount is at least $1.00.
2. The transaction is no more than 60 days old, compared with get_time.
3. The linked checking account is OPEN.
4. The account tier's open-dispute limit has room left, counting existing open disputes plus the new ones. The tier comes from account_class.
If a rule fails for a transaction, tell the customer what blocks it and do not file that dispute.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_accounts","get_cards","get_transactions","get_dispute_status","get_time"],"after":["get_cards","get_transactions","get_dispute_status"],"if":null,"quote":"Customer cannot exceed the maximum open disputes for their checking account tier: Entry Tier max 2, Mid Tier max 3, Premium Tier max 4, Elite Tier max 5. Dispute limits are per account, not per customer.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"explain_limit_and_choose","by":"model","do":"If an account has fewer open-dispute slots left than the customer's requested disputes on it, explain the limit and how many more can be filed on that account now, then ask which disputes to file now. File only that many, in the customer's order. The rest can be filed once existing disputes on that account close, as long as each transaction is still no more than 60 days old.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["check_prefiling","get_dispute_status"],"after":["check_prefiling"],"if":"the requested disputes on an account exceed its remaining open-dispute slots","quote":"Customer cannot exceed the maximum open disputes for their checking account tier: Entry Tier max 2, Mid Tier max 3, Premium Tier max 4, Elite Tier max 5. Dispute limits are per account, not per customer.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"limit per account by tier","quote":"Customer cannot exceed the maximum open disputes for their checking account tier: Entry Tier max 2, Mid Tier max 3, Premium Tier max 4, Elite Tier max 5. Dispute limits are per account, not per customer.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"the customer chooses which to file first","source":"none","why":"No document says how to choose among disputes when the limit applies, so the agent asks the customer."},{"clause":"later filing still needs the 60-day age rule","quote":"Transaction must be within 60 days old","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]},{"id":"gather_details","by":"model","do":"For each dispute, ask for anything the customer has not said: transaction type, discovery date, card in possession, PIN compromised, merchant contact (non-fraud disputes), and police report (fraud over $500).
- ATM dispute: also ask whether it was a Rho-Bank or a third-party ATM, and how much cash was actually dispensed (for a deposit, how much was deposited).
