utes.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"alert_card_no_clear","by":"model","do":"If the disputed card has a customer-initiated fraud alert and the customer denied a transaction in the alert review, do not clear the alert. The card's action follows decide_card_action. If the card is closed, tell the customer the alert stays on the closed card. If a replacement is ordered, tell them they will use the replacement.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["decide_card_action","get_cards"],"after":["decide_card_action"],"if":"the dispute came from a fraud-alert transaction review in which the customer denied a transaction","quote":"If they confirm all transactions are legitimate, clear the alert.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003","basis":[{"clause":"do not clear","quote":"If fraud_alert_active is TRUE and alert_source is 'customer_initiated' → Ask customer to verify recent transactions. If they confirm all transactions are legitimate, clear the alert.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003"},{"clause":"card action from decide_card_action","quote":"when performing the actual card action after filing all disputes, use the MOST SEVERE action across all disputes","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"replacement only if ordered","quote":"Ask if they want to order a replacement card immediately","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"}]},{"id":"deferred_dispute_no_card_action","by":"model","do":"A dispute held back by the open-dispute limit (or any other rule) was not filed, so its category sets no card action now. Decide each card's action only from its disputes actually filed. If all filed disputes on that card map to keep_active, leave the card active. Do not push a freeze or closure the customer did not ask for. Tell the customer the held-back dispute can be filed once an open dispute on that account closes.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["explain_limit_and_choose","file_dispute","decide_card_action"],"after":["decide_card_action"],"if":"a dispute the customer raised on a card was held back and not filed","quote":"When filing multiple disputes for the same card, record each dispute's card_action based on its own category mapping (do NOT change individual dispute parameters).","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"deferred_dispute_on_closed_card","by":"model","do":"A dispute held back by the open-dispute limit may be on a card that is then closed in this conversation because of another filed fraud dispute. Tell the customer the held-back dispute can still be filed later on that checking account, once an open dispute there closes; the card being closed does not stop that. Do not file it now.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["explain_limit_and_choose","count_open_disputes","close_card"],"after":["close_card"],"if":"a dispute was held back by the open-dispute limit on a card that was then closed for close_and_reissue","quote":"Dispute limits are per account, not per customer.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"id":"freeze_card","by":"harness","do":"Before freezing, tell the customer:
