1. The card's user_id matches the verified user.
2. The card's status is ACTIVE or PENDING. If it is FROZEN, unfreeze_before_close runs first. If it is CLOSED, no closure is needed.
3. There are no pending transactions (status 'pending' in get_transactions).
4. There are no pending refunds. If one exists, the customer can wait for it to process (typically 3-5 business days). Or they can acknowledge in writing in this conversation that it will be credited to the linked checking account instead; if they do, check 4 passes.
The 14-day minimum card age does not apply to lost, stolen or fraud_suspected. If check 1, 3 or 4 fails, tell the customer what must be resolved, and do not unfreeze or close the card.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["get_cards","get_transactions","check_identity"],"after":["decide_card_action"],"if":"the most severe action for the card is close_and_reissue","quote":"Check eligibility requirements. If any requirement is not met, inform the customer what needs to be resolved and do not proceed with closure.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"id":"unfreeze_before_close","by":"harness","do":"The card must be closed, but its status is FROZEN, and closing requires ACTIVE or PENDING. First check in get_accounts that the linked checking account is OPEN. Tell the customer the card will be briefly reactivated only so it can be closed right away. Then unlock unfreeze_debit_card_3893, call it for the card, and go straight on to close_card. If the linked account is not OPEN, or the unfreeze returns an error, do not close the card: explain this and follow transfer_if_needed.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"unfreeze_debit_card_3893","card_id":"the card_id from get_cards"},"lookup":["get_cards","get_accounts","close_eligibility_check","decide_card_action"],"after":["close_eligibility_check"],"if":"the most severe action for the card is close_and_reissue, its status in get_cards is FROZEN, the linked checking account is OPEN, and checks 1, 3 and 4 of close_eligibility_check passed","quote":"Use unfreeze_debit_card_3893 with the card_id","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"id":"close_card","by":"harness","do":"Tell the customer the card will be permanently deactivated and any pending transactions will still be processed. Unlock close_debit_card_4721 and call it, with reason 'lost' or 'stolen' if the customer reported the card so (lost_card_fraud_branch), otherwise 'fraud_suspected'. After closing, tell the customer:
- the card cannot be reactivated;
- any recurring payments linked to it need new payment information.
For fraud_suspected, recommend they also change their online banking password.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"close_debit_card_4721","card_id":"the card_id from get_cards","reason":"lost or stolen if the customer reported it so; otherwise fraud_suspected"},"lookup":["decide_card_action","get_cards","close_eligibility_check"],"after":["decide_card_action","close_eligibility_check","unfreeze_before_close"],"if":"the most severe action for the card is close_and_reissue AND close_eligibility_check passed AND the card status is ACTIVE or PENDING (directly, or after unfreeze_before_close succeeded for a FROZEN card)","quote":"5. Use close_debit_card_4721 to close the card with parameters: card_id, reason","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025","basis":[{"clause":"close with card_id and reason","quote":"5. Use close_debit_card_4721 to close the card with parameters: card_id, reason","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"pending transactions still processed","quote":"Inform customer that any pending transactions will still be processed","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"permanently deactivated","quote":"The card is now permanently deactivated and cannot be reactivated","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"recurring payments need updating","quote":"Any recurring payments linked to this card will need to be updated with new payment information","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"password for fraud_suspected","quote":"For fraud_suspected closures, recommend the customer also change their online banking password","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"}]},{"id":"replacement_entry_wait","by":"model","do":"If the closed card's checking account is Entry tier (Light Blue, Light Green, Green Fee-Free), tell the customer a replacement can be ordered only 48 hours after the closure, and give the earliest time from get_time. Do not call order_debit_card_5739 now. Entry tier ships standard only ($0).","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["close_card","get_accounts","get_time"],"after":["close_card"],"if":"a card was closed in this conversation, the customer wants a replacement, and its account is Entry tier","quote":"48-hour waiting period after card closure before a replacement can be ordered","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"id":"order_replacement","by":"model","do":"Ask whether the customer wants a replacement card. If yes:
1. Check the ordering requirements from get_accounts, get_cards and the verified record:
   - the account is OPEN and has been open at least 3 business days;
   - the balance is at least $25 and covers the fees;
   - there is no other ACTIVE card and no PENDING card or order on the account;
   - the customer is at least 18;
   - the address is a US domestic address.
   If one fails, explain it and stop.
2. Count replacements (issue_reason lost, stolen, fraud or damaged) issued in the last 12 months. If the tier limit is reached:
   - Entry or Mid: the customer can wait until the oldest ages out, or pay the excess fee ($25 Entry, $15 Mid). Order only if they choose to pay.
   - Premium: they must wait.
   - Elite: no limit.
3. Ask for the delivery option and design, and state the tier's fees.
4. Confirm the mailing address.
5. Tell the customer the fees will be deducted from the checking account.
6. Unlock order_debit_card_5739 and call it.
7. Tell the customer the expected delivery timeframe and the fees charged. If the order returns an error, explain the stated requirement and stop.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"order_debit_card_5739","account_id":"the linked checking account from get_cards","user_id":"the verified user's id","delivery_option":"STANDARD, EXPEDITED or RUSH, as the customer chose within the tier's allowed options (Entry: STANDARD only)","card_design":"CLASSIC, PREMIUM or CUSTOM, as the customer chose","delivery_fee":"from the tier rules for the chosen delivery option (doc 029)","design_fee":"from the tier rules for the chosen design (doc 029)","shipping_address":"the full mailing address the customer confirmed (address on file, or an alternate the customer gave)","excess_replacement_fee":"$25 (Entry) or $15 (Mid) only if the limit is reached and the customer chose to pay it; otherwise omit"},"lookup":["close_card","get_accounts","get_cards"],"after":["close_card"],"if":"a card was closed in close_card AND the customer wants a replacement AND the ordering requirements and the tier's replacement rules allow it (no Entry-tier 48-hour wait pending; within the limit, or the customer pays the Entry/Mid excess fee)","quote":"When using order_debit_card_5739, you must provide the exact delivery_fee and design_fee amounts based on the tier rules below.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029","basis":[{"clause":"ask whether they want a replacement","quote":"Ask if they want to order a replacement card immediately","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"minimum balance $25","quote":"Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"one active card","quote":"Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"no pending order","quote":"Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"open at least 3 business days","quote":"Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"age 18","quote":"Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"US address","quote":"Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"count replacements","quote":"Look for cards with issue_reason of 'lost', 'stolen', 'fraud', or 'damaged'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Entry limit: wait or $25","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 2-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out of the 12-month window, OR pay a $25 excess replacement fee","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Mid limit: wait or $15","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 3-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out, OR pay a $15 excess replacement fee","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Premium limit: wait only","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 5-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out (no fee option - must wait)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"confirm address","quote":"Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"fee deducted notice","quote":"Always inform the customer that the fee will be deducted from their checking account balance before placing the order.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"delivery timeframe and fees","quote":"Inform customer of expected delivery timeframe and any applicable fees","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"insufficient funds fails","quote":"If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"}]},{"id":"cross_product_handoff","by":"model","do":"After the card actions, if a card the customer reported lost or stolen was closed or frozen, run lost_stolen_card_cross_product_security_protocol: check for Rho-Bank credit cards and offer a replacement.","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["lost_card_fraud_branch","close_card"],"after":["close_card","freeze_card"],"if":"a card the customer reported lost or stolen was closed or frozen","quote":"Complete the standard debit card freeze/close procedure","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_030"},{"id":"confirm_filed","by":"model","do":"Confirm each filed dispute. For each one, give the customer:
- its category;
- whether provisional credit applies: the full amount, reduced by $50 or $500 if reported late, issued within 10 business days (20 for accounts under 30 days old), or immediately for a confirmed Rho-Bank ATM cash discrepancy;
- the investigation timeline:
  - with provisional credit, 45 business days (90 for international, foreign POS or new accounts);
  - third-party ATM, up to 90 days;
  - Rho-Bank ATM deposit, up to 45 days;
  - otherwise typically 10 to 45 business days;
- any affidavit due within 10 business days;
- the card action.
