ve no pending transactions before closure","quote":"4. No pending transactions: The card must not have any pending or processing transactions.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"rule":"An Entry-tier replacement cannot be ordered until 48 hours after closure","quote":"48-hour waiting period after card closure before a replacement can be ordered","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"rule":"A replacement order needs a minimum balance of $25 on the account","quote":"Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"rule":"Any date the workflow needs, including 'today' as a discovery date, comes from get_current_time","quote":"If you need the current time, always use the get_current_time() tool.","doc":"policy"},{"rule":"Transfer reason codes are chosen from the highest tier that applies","quote":"Reasons are organized into 4 priority tiers - always select from the highest tier that applies.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_042"},{"rule":"Unauthorized transactions and fraud map to the Tier 1 reason code fraud_or_security_concern","quote":"Fraud, identity theft, unauthorized transactions, or security concerns requiring specialist handling","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_042"},{"rule":"An existing dispute past its regulatory timelines is escalated to a supervisor","quote":"If a dispute appears to be exceeding timelines, escalate to a supervisor.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_035"},{"rule":"discovery_date is the date the customer first noticed the issue","quote":"Date customer first noticed the issue.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"rule":"A PIN-locked card that cannot be unlocked and has successful unauthorized transactions gets a dispute for each one, then closure and replacement","quote":"If unauthorized transactions found: File dispute, close card, order replacement.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"rule":"A PIN-locked card with only declined attempts gets no dispute","quote":"If no unauthorized transactions: Explain the security concern and offer options:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_041"},{"rule":"Each disputed transaction is filed under its own transaction_id","quote":"ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"rule":"A Rho-Bank ATM cash claim is checked against the transaction record (the journal) before filing","quote":"View recent transactions on the corresponding checking accounts to pull ATM journal records for the transaction","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"rule":"If the Rho-Bank ATM record shows the right amount was dispensed, the claim cannot be validated. The customer may still file it, or drop it.","quote":"If journal shows correct amount dispensed, inform customer the claim cannot be validated but they may still file a formal dispute","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"}],"done_when":"All of the following hold:
- The customer is verified and the verification is logged (once per conversation).
- Every requested dispute that passes the pre-filing rules and fits the account's open-dispute limit has been filed, one per transaction_id. Existing open disputes, and disputes filed earlier in this conversation, were counted per account. When the limit applied, the customer chose the order.
- Disputes held back, dropped, or already on file have been explained, and they set no card action.
- Each card's most severe action among its filed disputes has been performed once, after the last dispute: freeze, close (plus a replacement if wanted and allowed, or the Entry-tier 48-hour wait explained), or nothing for keep_active.
- If a lost or stolen card was closed, the cross-product check has been handed off.
